WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.786 --> 00:00:17.847
Thornfield was now a merry place.

2
00:00:19.128 --> 00:00:24.593
Every evening the guests gathered in the sitting room to talk or play games while I watched Mr.

3
00:00:24.673 --> 00:00:28.196
Rochester and Blanche Ingram from my place on the window seat.

4
00:00:29.477 --> 00:00:32.159
I've told you, reader, that I'd learned to love Mr.

5
00:00:32.219 --> 00:00:37.919
Rochester. I could not stop loving him now merely because he'd ceased to notice me.

6
00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:43.783
I was not jealous of Miss Ingram; she was too inferior to excite that feeling.

7
00:00:44.883 --> 00:00:47.665
She was very showy, but her mind was poor.

8
00:00:48.886 --> 00:00:53.829
She never had an opinion of her own, and she was often needlessly cruel to Adele.

9
00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:56.051
I realized that Mr.

10
00:00:56.111 --> 00:01:00.954
Rochester was going to marry her, perhaps for family or political reasons.

11
00:01:02.155 --> 00:01:03.836
But I felt that he did not love her.

12
00:01:04.896 --> 00:01:08.438
What upset me was that she didn't know how to charm him and I did.

13
00:01:09.639 --> 00:01:15.823
If she'd sat quietly by his side, instead of accosting him with brilliant remarks, she might have won

14
00:01:15.883 --> 00:01:16.363
his love.

15
00:01:18.324 --> 00:01:22.787
Meanwhile I grew lenient toward my master, forgetting all his faults.

16
00:01:24.268 --> 00:01:26.589
One wet afternoon the guests were restless.

17
00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:31.372
Mr. Rochester had ridden out earlier and had not yet returned.

18
00:01:32.544 --> 00:01:37.326
The ladies had proposed visiting a Gypsy camp, but that was postponed due to the weather.

19
00:01:38.507 --> 00:01:42.468
It was almost dusk, and Adele was kneeling by me on the window seat.

20
00:01:42.488 --> 00:01:44.129
"Here's Mr.

21
00:01:44.189 --> 00:01:47.430
Rochester!" she cried as a carriage came up the drive.

22
00:01:48.611 --> 00:01:52.052
Blanche Ingram hurried to the window, almost falling over me.

23
00:01:53.233 --> 00:01:55.594
With a sneer she moved to another window.

24
00:01:55.614 --> 00:01:57.494
"That's not Mr.

25
00:01:57.614 --> 00:02:00.956
Rochester, you tiresome little monkey," she said to Adele.

26
00:02:02.048 --> 00:02:04.390
"Who perched you up there to give false intelligence?"

27
00:02:05.571 --> 00:02:08.194
She glanced angrily at me as if I were to blame.

28
00:02:10.076 --> 00:02:12.658
A servant soon brought the stranger to the sitting room.

29
00:02:13.819 --> 00:02:17.382
He bowed to Lady Ingram as she was the eldest lady present.

30
00:02:17.402 --> 00:02:21.947
"It seems that I've come at a bad time, madam, when my friend, Mr.

31
00:02:22.007 --> 00:02:24.049
Rochester, is away," said the man.

32
00:02:24.069 --> 00:02:30.033
"But I arrive from a very long journey, and I think I may presume on such an old,

33
00:02:30.073 --> 00:02:33.174
intimate acquaintance as to remain here until he returns."

34
00:02:34.374 --> 00:02:36.154
He was a handsome man about Mr.

35
00:02:36.194 --> 00:02:39.775
Rochester's age, but something about him repelled me.

36
00:02:40.876 --> 00:02:42.656
I soon learned that he was Mr.

37
00:02:42.716 --> 00:02:45.857
Mason and that he'd just arrived from Jamaica.

38
00:02:46.857 --> 00:02:48.518
I was wondering how he knew Mr.

39
00:02:48.598 --> 00:02:54.759
Rochester when a servant announced that an old Gypsy woman had arrived and wanted to tell the fortunes

40
00:02:54.819 --> 00:02:56.340
of the young, single ladies.

41
00:02:57.468 --> 00:03:02.492
She refused to come into the sitting room, insisting that they come to her in the library.

42
00:03:04.353 --> 00:03:07.815
Miss Ingram went first, laughing gaily as she left us.

43
00:03:08.996 --> 00:03:14.880
When she returned, she refused to say what the Gypsy had told her and flounced onto a couch

44
00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:18.342
with a book, which she looked at moodily without turning a page.

45
00:03:19.523 --> 00:03:23.566
Her sister, Mary, went next accompanied by the Eshton sisters.

46
00:03:24.706 --> 00:03:26.728
They returned shrieking and laughing.

47
00:03:27.836 --> 00:03:29.337
"She knows all about us!"

48
00:03:29.817 --> 00:03:30.498
they cried.

49
00:03:31.658 --> 00:03:34.780
While I was watching them, a servant appeared at my side.

50
00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:41.924
"If you please, miss, the Gypsy says there's another young, single lady and she refuses to leave until

51
00:03:41.984 --> 00:03:42.764
she sees you."

52
00:03:43.905 --> 00:03:47.366
When I entered the library, the Gypsy was sitting by the hearth.

53
00:03:48.607 --> 00:03:54.550
She wore a red cloak and a wide-brimmed, black hat tied under her chin with a striped handkerchief.

54
00:03:55.791 --> 00:04:00.858
The hat brim shaded her face, the lower part of which was concealed by a white scarf.

55
00:04:00.878 --> 00:04:03.941
"Do you want your fortune told?"

56
00:04:04.381 --> 00:04:05.962
she asked in a harsh voice.

57
00:04:05.982 --> 00:04:11.387
"I don't care, but I must warn you I don't believe in fortunes."

58
00:04:11.407 --> 00:04:16.030
"You're impudent to say so, but I expected that of you."

59
00:04:16.050 --> 00:04:21.855
I was not impressed with her, but I let her rattle on about my health and other things

60
00:04:21.895 --> 00:04:23.156
she thought she knew about me.

61
00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:25.861
When she began to talk of Mr.

62
00:04:25.942 --> 00:04:30.565
Rochester, I was still skeptical, but I thought I'd try a question of my own.

63
00:04:30.586 --> 00:04:32.167
"Is Mr.

64
00:04:32.247 --> 00:04:33.608
Rochester getting married?"

65
00:04:34.048 --> 00:04:34.549
I asked.

66
00:04:34.569 --> 00:04:38.332
"Yes, to the beautiful Blanche Ingram."

67
00:04:39.493 --> 00:04:42.035
"Soon?" "It appears so.

68
00:04:43.196 --> 00:04:46.759
He must love such a handsome, witty, accomplished lady.

69
00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:51.964
And she probably loves him or, if not him, at least his fortune."

70
00:04:53.096 --> 00:04:54.997
Here the Gypsy smiled to herself.

71
00:04:55.017 --> 00:05:02.600
"I know she considers his fortune very desirable, although I told her something about that which made her

72
00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:06.261
frown." "But I didn't come to hear Mr.

73
00:05:06.341 --> 00:05:07.462
Rochester's fortune.

74
00:05:08.602 --> 00:05:09.743
I came to hear my own."

75
00:05:10.883 --> 00:05:17.106
The Gypsy beckoned me to come closer, and suddenly I noticed a ring on her finger, a ring

76
00:05:17.166 --> 00:05:19.367
that I'd seen a hundred times before.

77
00:05:19.387 --> 00:05:21.548
"Mr. Rochester!"

78
00:05:22.832 --> 00:05:23.392
I cried.

79
00:05:24.573 --> 00:05:26.133
He laughed and took off his hat.

80
00:05:26.153 --> 00:05:28.674
"Do you forgive me, Jane?"

81
00:05:28.695 --> 00:05:32.296
"I'll try, but it wasn't right to fool the ladies."

82
00:05:32.316 --> 00:05:34.637
"Ah, the ladies."

83
00:05:35.817 --> 00:05:38.358
Mr. Rochester removed his cloak as he stood up.

84
00:05:39.559 --> 00:05:41.620
"What are they discussing in the sitting room?"

85
00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:45.041
"They're probably talking about the Gypsy, sir.

86
00:05:46.162 --> 00:05:48.142
But do you know that a stranger has arrived?"

87
00:05:49.283 --> 00:05:50.063
He shook his head.

88
00:05:50.083 --> 00:05:51.624
"Who is it?"

89
00:05:52.692 --> 00:05:56.255
"He comes from the island of Jamaica, sir, and his name is Mason."

90
00:05:58.156 --> 00:05:59.477
"Mason! Jamaica!"

91
00:06:00.618 --> 00:06:04.801
Mr. Rochester grasped my wrist convulsively and his smile froze.

92
00:06:04.821 --> 00:06:06.942
"Are you ill, sir?"

93
00:06:08.223 --> 00:06:10.385
I was concerned because he'd turned so white.

94
00:06:10.405 --> 00:06:12.886
"I've suffered a blow, Jane."

95
00:06:13.267 --> 00:06:13.927
He staggered.

96
00:06:13.947 --> 00:06:16.589
"Oh! Lean on me, sir."

97
00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:20.552
I helped him sit down, and he made me sit beside him.

98
00:06:21.768 --> 00:06:26.131
Holding my hand in both of his, he gazed at me in a most distressed way.

99
00:06:26.151 --> 00:06:28.253
"My little friend!"

100
00:06:28.633 --> 00:06:29.053
he said.

101
00:06:29.073 --> 00:06:35.958
"I wish I were on a quiet island with only you, and that trouble, danger, and all hideous

102
00:06:36.018 --> 00:06:37.859
recollections were removed from me."

103
00:06:39.140 --> 00:06:39.921
I was alarmed.

104
00:06:39.941 --> 00:06:41.722
"Can I help you?

105
00:06:42.743 --> 00:06:44.224
I'd give my life to serve you."

106
00:06:44.244 --> 00:06:45.965
"Thank you, Jane.

107
00:06:46.205 --> 00:06:49.648
If all the fine people in the sitting room came here and spat at me, what would you

108
00:06:49.688 --> 00:06:53.313
do?" "Turn them out of the room if I could."

109
00:06:53.333 --> 00:06:58.116
"But what if I tried to talk to them and they only sneered at me and whispered among

110
00:06:58.156 --> 00:07:00.978
themselves? What if they abandoned me?

111
00:07:02.099 --> 00:07:02.899
Would you go with them?"

112
00:07:02.919 --> 00:07:04.901
"Oh no, sir.

113
00:07:05.881 --> 00:07:07.822
I'd rather stay and try to comfort you."

114
00:07:07.842 --> 00:07:11.225
"Could you risk their disapproval for my sake?"

115
00:07:12.325 --> 00:07:16.148
"I'd do it for anyone who deserves my friendship, as I'm sure you do."

116
00:07:17.376 --> 00:07:20.159
He asked me to go into the sitting room and whisper to Mr.

117
00:07:20.199 --> 00:07:22.961
Mason that he was wanted in the library by Mr.

118
00:07:23.021 --> 00:07:25.944
Rochester. I did as he asked.

119
00:07:27.145 --> 00:07:32.750
Later that night as I was falling asleep, I heard him talking happily as he showed Mason to

120
00:07:32.790 --> 00:07:33.290
a bedroom.

121
00:07:34.471 --> 00:07:39.075
Mr. Rochester's cheerful tone set my heart at ease, and I was soon asleep.
